  "structuring": {
    "prompt_additions": "Georgia uses ARTICLE (მუხლი) as the basic unit, not SECTION. Higher divisions are CHAPTER (თავი) for ordinary laws, and BOOK (წიგნი) > CHAPTER for codes (Civil Code has 5 books: I General Provisions, II Family, III Property, IV Obligations, V Inheritance). Article numbering is continuous throughout the document — do not restart per chapter. First-level subdivisions within articles use PARAGRAPH with Arabic numeral enumeration (1),(2),(3). Second-level subdivisions use SUBPARAGRAPH with Georgian alphabetic enumeration (ა,ბ,გ,დ…). For eIds, transliterate Georgian letters using ISO 9984: ა→a, ბ→b, გ→g, დ→d, ე→e, ვ→v, ზ→z, თ→t, ი→i, კ→k, ლ→l, მ→m, ნ→n, ო→o, პ→p. Inserted articles (5¹, 5²) become art_5-1, art_5-2 in eIds. Detect 'კოდექსი' in document title and use BOOK-level hierarchy variant."
  },
